Methodology paper about outcome reporting bias |
| 20 | Effects of deep and superficial heating in the management of frozen shoulder | Abstract describes MS study, not 
frozen shoulder |
| 23 | The natural history of the frozen shoulder syndrome | Observational natural history study, not RCT |
| 24 | Quantifying heterogeneity in meta‐analysis | Methodology paper about meta-analysis statistics |
| 25 | Chapter 10: Addressing reporting biases | Book chapter, not primary study |

**RATIONALE FOR KEY DECISIONS:**

**Included studies met all criteria:**
- Randomised controlled trials (RCTs) or quasi-randomised trials
- Adults with adhesive capsulitis/frozen shoulder
- Comparing manual therapy (mobilisation, manipulation) or exercise interventions
- Measuring relevant outcomes (pain, ROM, function)

**Excluded studies failed criteria:**
- Not RCTs (observational, case reports, methodology papers)
- Not primary studies (systematic reviews, book chapters)
- Wrong population (multiple sclerosis instead of frozen shoulder)
- Wrong study type (questionnaire validation, prevalence studies)

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
- Studies 9, 16, and 18 were assigned medium confidence because the abstracts did not explicitly confirm randomisation 
but appeared to be comparative trials with relevant interventions
- Study 20 was excluded due to title-abstract mismatch (title mentions frozen shoulder but abstract describes multiple 
sclerosis study)
- Conservative approach applied: when in doubt about study design, studies were included for further review

