There were three consecutive stages: pain, stiffness, and recovery. The stiffness stage was usually related to the 
duration of the recovery stage. The total duration was longer than is generally supposed (an average total of 30.1 
months in contrast to about 18 months as often postulated). Generally speaking, the longer the stiffness stage is, the 
longer is the recovery stage. In 4 patients the second shoulder became similarly affected, 6 months to 7 years after the
